WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
NFI RAG: measuring retrieval on a small public-literature pilot. Changes are under review; this is not a production accuracy claim.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:40.000
The dashboard exposes both evaluation splits, configuration comparisons, source labels, and retrieved passages.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:01:00.000
On 24 held-out questions, hybrid retrieved the labeled paper in the top three for 20. Context expansion reached 24; reranking improved order.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:20.000
One failure: a vague follow-up lost the earlier gluten-free bread topic. Hybrid retrieval returned papers other than the labeled source.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Bounded context expansion restored the prior user topic. The same question then retrieved the labeled paper first.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Trade-offs: preserve source governance, keep reranking optional, and require expert review before reporting answer quality. Next: live-corpus evaluation.
